NextBSD: give the CMake-built library the upstream soname.

libxml2 2.9.13's CMakeLists.txt sets VERSION but no SOVERSION, so CMake
uses the full version as the soname (libxml2.so.2.9.13). The autotools
build, and every distribution, ship libxml2.so.2. Upstream fixed this in
2.10 in the same way.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -489,6 +489,7 @@
 	OUTPUT_NAME xml2
 	POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON
 	PREFIX lib
+	SOVERSION ${LIBXML_MAJOR_VERSION}
 	VERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION}
 )
 
